Janis Papanagnou <Janis_Papanagnou@hotmail.com> writes:
> I've got a longworm with these stats and was wondering whether it's
> intentional and usually possible that these worms gets 205 maxHP or
> whether it could be some bug (I saw that worm in The Wizards tower)
> 
>    Status of the long worm (neutral):  Level 12  HP 47(205)  AC 5.
> 
> At least I cannot remember to have seen such tough long worms before.

Long worms with sufficient room to grow in length will do so every
d15+2 turns and gain 3 HP in the process, raising max HP if necessary;
conversely, a worm that runs into a dead end or traps itself in its
own tail will shrink a segment and lose 3 HP, but its max HP is _not_
lowered. This process caps at 500 HP, after which point new segments
will still be added if there's room but HP will cease to increase.

